What this covers
----------------
The database is the set of records produced by this project's connectors and
pipeline: the `program` table, its junction tables (`program_applicant_type`,
`program_category`, `program_aln`), the `run` and `program_change` logs, and
every export built from them (the published site's embedded JSON and the
`atlas.db` file it links to). The code that builds and renders the database is
separately licensed under the MIT License (see LICENSE).

What this does not claim
------------------------
Program names, summaries, deadlines and eligibility text are public government
text read from the source pages and federal APIs named in each record's
`source_url`. They are republished verbatim with that attribution and no
ownership is asserted over them. Nothing in the database is advice; a record's
status and dates are what its source said on the run date recorded alongside it.

